  **Coverage of the four focus questions:**

  Q1 （广州 as domestic relay when DMIT blocked by GFW): GFW IP blocking is destination-based; from 广州 Tencent egress, TCP to DMIT IP would also be dropped. Evidence today: ping OK, SSH timeout — classic GFW TCP-drop signature. So the planned primary relay leg fails exactly in the scenario it must cover. Only the GIA path （广州→66云→DMIT or 广州→66云 endpoint) survives, because GIA IP isn't blocked. So the relay should target GIA, not DMIT. Plan lists GIA as backup — should be flipped: GIA relay primary, DMIT direct secondary. Also, better: make 广州 terminate device tunnels itself (hub), removing international leg from the management path entirely — that's what "国内服务器单独作为控制服务器" actually means per user's words.

  Q2 (ping通 SSH超时 root cause): explain GFW mechanics: IP blocked → TCP SYN dropped (all ports or specific), ICMP usually passes. Differential diagnosis: (a) GFW IP block (most likely given today's event and same signature from both PC and Tencent); (b) DMIT firewall/fail2ban blocking Tencent range (check DMIT side: other sources OK?); (c) Tencent outbound filtering. Tests: from 广州， tcping DMIT ports 22/28722/8444/others; from a second domestic network; from GIA/abroad. If all domestic sources fail all TCP ports while foreign sources succeed → GFW IP block. If only Tencent fails → DMIT-side ACL/fail2ban. Also check whether PC→DMIT fails on all ports similarly.

  Q3 (new SPOF): 
  - 广州 single domestic relay (no second domestic node) — acceptable while additive, but once 应急包 points only to 广州， failure of 广州 + international outage = total loss; mitigate by keeping GIA target as alternate in kit.
  - DMIT backend remains SPOF for the management plane (hub 10.10.0.1:8443, platform, heartbeat DB, WG hub on DO too!). Wait — WG hub on DO, DO kept until 11-02. MGMT_TARGET=10.10.0.1:8443 — whose 8443? The mgmt backend. On DMIT now presumably (management API on DMIT, reachable via WG 10.10.0.1 from VPSs?). The -L target resolution happens on the endpoint VPS. If the hub network (WG, hub on DO) is involved, then DO retirement on 11-02 interacts: does 10.10.0.1 live on DO's WG? AGENTS.md: "医院通道和 WireGuard hub 仍在 DO". So the -L target 10.10.0.1:8443 is reachable via the WG network hubbed at DO! Then when DO retires 2026-11-02 (4 days away), every -L management channel dies unless hub migrates. The plan completely ignores this coupling —广州 relay to "DMIT 后端" via SSH on 8443 is actually a different path （广州 SSH to DMIT:8443? diagram says SSH 接力：8443 → DMIT 后端）. Hmm, 8444 is the mgmt console port per AGENTS.md (8444). The diagram says "SSH 接力：8443". Ambiguity worth flagging. Anyway: the plan must specify where 广州's relay terminates and how it reaches the mgmt API if WG hub moves.

  - Also PC→management: plan focuses on device→hub, but user's own access (PC→DMIT 8444 console, PC→device via 1322x ports) also dies when DMIT blocked. The plan must include PC-side access via 广州 (e.g., PC→广州→GIA→DMIT 8444, or mirror reverse ports on 广州）. 方案.md doesn't address user-side access path at all. Actually 架构评估 section 六 doesn't either. Gap.

  Q4 (safe ordering given DMIT unreachable from PC today):
  Current reachability matrix (from R5 diagnostic + today's events): PC→DO:28722 works (login success). PC→DMIT intermittent. DO/GIA health 200. Devices have live -L sessions to DO/GIA (R5 had SSH inbound sessions from its site IP). So today's working management path: PC→DO (or PC→GIA? unclear, DMIT→GIA had key auth failures) → via WG hub on DO → device -L channels... but -L only gives agent API/heartbeat access from device side; server→device SSH needs -R on some endpoint. R5's -R on DMIT dead (no listen 13225). Hmm.

  Safe ordering recommendation:
  0. Freeze: no device changes until a verified PC→device path exists that does not depend on DMIT-from-PC. Today that candidate is PC→DO:28722→（现有连接） or via GIA.
